# Web Development - Modern Theme & Component Patterns

## Theme & Style

- **Design system**: Radix UI + shadcn/ui (radix-nova style)
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS with CSS variables (--primary, --foreground, --muted, --border, --card)
- **Aesthetic**: Modern, clean, accessible. Use semantic colors (text-foreground, text-muted-foreground, bg-card, border-border)
- **Animations**: Use tailwindcss-animate (accordion-up, accordion-down, etc.)

## Component Mapping

When the prompt mentions these concepts, use the corresponding pattern:

| Prompt keywords | Use component | Reference |
|-----------------|---------------|-----------|
| accordion, FAQ, expandable, collapsible sections, reveal content | Accordion | See accordion reference below |
| tabs, tabbed interface | Tabs | @/components/ui/tabs |
| cards, card layout | Card | @/components/ui/card |
| dialog, modal | Dialog | @/components/ui/dialog |
| dropdown, menu | DropdownMenu | @/components/ui/dropdown-menu |

## Accordion Reference (FAQ / Expandable Sections)

**Import:**
```tsx
import {
  Accordion,
  AccordionContent,
  AccordionItem,
  AccordionTrigger,
} from "@/components/ui/accordion"
```

**Basic usage (single item open):**
```tsx
<Accordion type="single" collapsible defaultValue="item-1">
  <AccordionItem value="item-1">
    <AccordionTrigger>Is it accessible?</AccordionTrigger>
    <AccordionContent>
      Yes. It adheres to the WAI-ARIA design pattern.
    </AccordionContent>
  </AccordionItem>
</Accordion>
```

**FAQ-style with bordered cards:**
```tsx
<Accordion type="single" collapsible className="space-y-3">
  {items.map((item, i) => (
    <AccordionItem
      key={i}
      value={`item-${i}`}
      className="rounded-lg border border-border bg-card px-6 transition-colors hover:border-primary/30"
    >
      <AccordionTrigger className="text-left text-sm font-semibold text-foreground hover:no-underline">
        {item.question}
      </AccordionTrigger>
      <AccordionContent className="text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
        {item.answer}
      </AccordionContent>
    </AccordionItem>
  ))}
</Accordion>
```

**Multiple items open:** Use `type="multiple"` on Accordion.

**Install:** `npx shadcn@latest add accordion` (or component already at `src/components/ui/accordion.tsx`)

## Rule

When implementing web UI from a prompt:
1. Match prompt intent to the component mapping above
2. Use the exact import paths and patterns from this rule
3. Preserve semantic styling (foreground, muted-foreground, card, border-border)
4. Add accordion animations via `data-[state=closed]:animate-accordion-up data-[state=open]:animate-accordion-down` (already in AccordionContent)
